  "content": {
    "title": "Lucha Brothers Announce They Will Reunite At Triplemania: \"The Best Tag Team In The Universe\"",
    "text": "Penta and Rey Fenix announced at AAA Rey de Reyes on Saturday night that the Lucha Brothers are reuniting and will team up again at Triplemania. The segment opened with Fenix welcoming the crowd in Puebla and promising surprises. He then introduced his brother, WWE Intercontinental Champion Penta, who came out to the ring to a major reaction.Pat McAfee says WWE is in a good spot without him. Fenix went to leave, but Penta told him to stay. Penta addressed the crowd and said the brothers were originally supposed to reunite sooner, but his injury forced Rey Mysterio to take his spot. He then asked Fenix directly if the fans would like to see the Lucha Brothers together again. The Puebla crowd chanted for them. Penta made it official. “If the Mexican fans want it, they can have it,” he said. “We were born in AAA and made in Mexico, and it’s time for our people to see us together one more time as the best tag team in the universe.” The brothers confirmed that the reunion would take place at Triplemania, AAA’s biggest annual event and the Mexican equivalent of WrestleMania. No specific opponent or match was announced. The Lucha Brothers have not teamed together in WWE or AAA since Penta signed with WWE in late 2024. Fenix followed him to WWE programming through AAA, but the two have not been paired as a team on screen. Their last run as a regular tag team was in AEW, where they held the AEW World Tag Team Championship and were considered one of the top teams in the company. They originally rose to prominence in AAA before gaining international recognition through their work in AEW and on the independent circuit. Penta Dedicates Intercontinental Championship to Mexico Penta also used the segment to dedicate the WWE Intercontinental Championship to the Mexican fans. “The title isn’t just mine. It’s for all of you who get up every day to work hard in life for your dreams,” he said. “It’s for representation for all the beautiful people who fight every day.” He announced that he would defend the Intercontinental Championship not only on Raw but also in Mexico, and told everyone in the back he would be waiting for challengers to step forward. Penta won the Intercontinental Championship from Dominik Mysterio on the March 2 episode of Raw. Corey Graves, JBL, and Rey Mysterio called the show from the announce position. The announce team sent well wishes to Konnan at the top of the broadcast.",
